- bugfix: 2026-11-14 6e195ff fix(dashboard): clean up embed timer and keydown
  listener after dialog close
  After closing the FHEMWEB dialog the fragment's refresh timer and Escape
  listener kept running and dereferenced the removed .vcc-embed element
  (TypeError: null is not an object on the plain detail page). document.body
  substitutions now go through vccRoot(), which returns a detached dummy node
  and deregisters the global timer and keydown listener once the fragment is
  gone. The embed auto-refresh also keeps the current fragment on non-OK HTTP
  responses instead of replacing it with an error page.
- change: 2026-11-14 4a2e54a Entwicklung VolvoConnect 1.1.2-dev
- documentation: 2026-11-14 9bef59b docs(volvo): document scoped _showDashboard
  dialog and embed edit=1 parameter
- bugfix: 2026-11-14 4303b2f fix(dashboard): bind edit buttons via listeners
  and neutralize FHEM theme form styles
  Follows the proven _showEntityConfig pattern:
  replace inline onclick (toggleEdit/saveDashboardConfig/toggleTileReorderMode)
  with addEventListener bindings; inline handlers broke inside the scoped embed
  fragment because the IIFE keeps functions non-global (ReferenceError:
    toggleEdit)
  reset box-shadow/border-radius/text-shadow/background-image/font on input and
  button so FHEMWEB theme rules (e.g. touchpad input shadows) cannot restyle
    rows
  saveDashboardConfig now posts to the real FHEMWEB path and sends the fwcsrf
    token
  embed auto-refresh keeps the editable state via data-editable and ?edit=1
- bugfix: 2026-11-14 efcbe2d fix(dashboard): deliver _showDashboard as scoped
  fragment like _showEntityConfig
  The FHEM dialog received the full standalone page (global body/h1/.tile CSS),
  which collided with the FHEMWEB stylesheet and flipped the layout after load.
  Now _showDashboard returns the scoped embed fragment (.vcc-embed) via
  VolvoConnect_EmbedFragment, the same technique _showEntityConfig uses.
  Reverts the symptom fixes that this replaces:
  inline !important accent styles per tile (back to nth-child custom
    properties)
  modal-only flex/overflow layout (restores max-width:1120px per design doc)
- bugfix: 2026-11-14 5530673 fix: apply tile accent colors as inline styles to
  prevent FHEM override after update
  The tile accent colors (green #52bd8b, orange #e3b953, blue #8ab6d1) were
  being overridden by FHEM's CSS after initial render. Fixed by:
  1. Removing nth-child CSS rules that relied on DOM position
  2. Computing accent color based on tile index (mod 3) at render time
  3. Applying color directly as inline style attribute on tile and h2 elements
  This ensures colors persist even when FHEM refreshes content or injects CSS.
- bugfix: 2026-11-14 4c198d4 fix(dashboard): hardcode tile accent colors with
  !important to override FHEM cascade
  Replace CSS custom properties with direct hex color codes
  Apply !important to every color rule individually
  Separate border-top-color rules by nth-child selector
  Ensure green (#52bd8b), orange (#e3b953), and blue (#8ab6d1) display
    correctly in FHEM modal
- bugfix: 2026-11-14 9840aeb fix(dashboard): force correct tile accent colors
  in FHEM modal
  Added !important to CSS custom properties (--tile-accent) to override FHEM
    cascade
  Added !important to border-top and h2 color properties
  Added universal box-sizing reset for .wrap and all children
  This ensures correct green/orange/blue tile accent colors display in both
